#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:55
#: 5ca43b026ef4410f8515ae32aa868422
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:56
#: 2ce9e9f1a73e4b30bd68ba2ddb363b8b
msgid "RC input is configured on UART6. It supports all RC protocols except PPM, FPort, and SBUS. See :ref:`Radio Control Systems <common-rc-systems>` for details for a specific RC system. :ref:`SERIAL6_PROTOCOL<SERIAL6_PROTOCOL>` is set to “23”, by default, to enable this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:58
#: 718298ea04ba434a9b5814234fb56853
msgid "FPort requires an external bi-directional inverter and connects to TX 6 with :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` set to \"7\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:59
#: bcae0158d6d54494937093f50997f076
msgid "CRSF requires a TX6 connection, in addition to RX6, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:60
#: b91cbbfc6e334ebcb8d57a7069d6f2b0
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to TX6 and automatically provides telemetry. Set :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` set to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:62
#: 8d8906d3dce8494081bcc2a41f46893f
msgid "SBUS can be directly connected to the SBUS pin which ties through an inverter to the RX2 pin.  :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` must be set to \"23\" and :ref:`SERIAL6_PROTOCOL<SERIAL6_PROTOCOL>`  must be changed to something else than \"23\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:64
#: 336cd7b290f1482083e2ca476703e7ae
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM. See `Radio Control Systems <https://ardupilot.org/plane/docs/common-rc-systems.html#common-rc-systems>`_ for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:67
#: 485e261404944e12b333e666cdbc2958
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:68
#: 36642710b71c4064ad898a4bbaaa98aa
msgid "The SpeedyBee F405 AIO supports OSD using :ref:`OSD_TYPE<OSD_TYPE>` =  1 (MAX7456 driver). The defaults are also setup to allow DJI Goggle OSD support on UART3. Both the internal analog OSD and the DisplayPort OSD can be used simultaneously by setting :ref:`OSD_TYPE2<OSD_TYPE2>` = 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:71
#: 8eff3029fa2743e69fd7eed10bb05491
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:72
#: 98b985a8a6d74ebc9bd5e32136d60388
msgid "The SpeedyBee F405 AIO supports up to 5 PWM outputs. The pads for motor output ESC1 to ESC4 on the above diagram are the first 4 outputs.All 5 outputs support DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:74
#: e8e8e3f826ca46b995dd379bfaf691c2
msgid "The PWM are in 3 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:76
#: fddf027178724c2a9fc509e62e266bee
msgid "PWM 1-2: Group 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:77
#: 3d51e4b335ac471aad4003aed63683f7
msgid "PWM 3-4: Group 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:78
#: 61f53129b8954a69bfcf2b170e58435a
msgid "LED: Group 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:80
#: 1826ef52bf65446c877a6b2e224e4f90
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot. PWM 1-4 support bidirectional dshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:85
#: 7a14cfa9f08a4d28b1a12369e9450c86
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405aio.rst:86
#: 204bf06c29904670b20a54191267b9b7
msgid "The board has a builtin voltage sensor. The voltage sensor can handle 2S to 6S LiPo batteries. The integrated ESC also provides a current sensor."
msgstr ""

